A Company you will be happy to grow with!

At InnoTech, it´s all about connecting people with business through technology.

We truly care about you, your happiness, and your well-being. We look for passionate people who are eager to learn, evolve, and grow with us - because growth is in our DNA. This commitment has been consistently recognized: we are proud to be a Great Place to Work for five consecutive years, to be one of the Best IT Companies in Portugal, and to be recognized as a Best Workplace Wellbeing. We are also proud to hold ISO 27001 and ISO 9001 certifications, reinforcing our commitment to information security, quality, and continuous improvement. For us, sustainability is not just a buzzword. Integrity, social responsibility, and people-first values guide everything we do. Join our team of 180+ InnoTechers and bring your talent as a Mid Data Analyst.

Your Mission Will Be:

Develop, maintain, and optimize business KPIs to support strategic decision-making;
Analyze data, assess business impacts, and translate insights into actionable conclusions;
Create reports, dashboards, visualizations, and supporting documentation for management decisions;
Support Product, Commercial, and Strategy teams through business intelligence analysis;
Automate reporting processes and monitor key indicators to identify trends and improvement opportunities.

You Will Need:

Minimum of 2 years of professional experience in similar Data Analyst, Business Intelligence, Reporting, or Analytics roles;
Experience with Business Intelligence tools such as Power BI, MicroStrategy, or equivalent platforms;
Advanced knowledge of Excel, Power Query, and Power Pivot for data analysis and transformation;
Experience in reporting automation, KPI development, and business data interpretation;
CPLP nationality or an EU work permit is required to facilitate employment.

Would Be Awesome If You Have:

BSc or MSc in Computer Science/Engineering, Information Technology, or related fields;
Knowledge of SQL in Oracle and Databricks environments, as well as experience working with multiple data sources;
Familiarity with Google Analytics, Google Data Studio, or similar analytics platforms;
Knowledge of Python for data analysis and processing tasks;
Experience in the payments industry, Business Intelligence, Planning, Reporting, or Competitive Intelligence areas.

What we offer:

Health-focused partnerships, including free mental health support;
25 days of vacation, including your birthday, Carnival, and a bridging day between Christmas and New Year;
Half a vacation day on your children's birthday and a school supplies voucher;
Petsitting partnerships and a pet bereavement day;
Regular team buildings, four annual company parties, game nights, and social events;
InnoSports initiatives (football, marathons, and more);
Events focused on sustainability and social responsibility actions.

Are you convinced? Come see it for yourself.

Join our Top-Notch Team!

